James sought guidance about a contract with a California solar company for his Philadelphia home due to the company's failure to perform. I explained that Pennsylvania law likely governs consumer protection issues related to the contract, despite the contract specifying California law and a Los Angeles venue for disputes. I advised him to examine clauses for jurisdiction and governing law, noting that Pennsylvania has strong consumer protections that could apply. Ultimately, I recommended consulting a Pennsylvania consumer-construction lawyer to assess his options without invoking litigation prematurely. We emphasized the importance of evidence and proper notices regarding contract termination to leverage his position effectively.
